{
  "_comment": [
    "pnpd: the Peios Network Policy daemon — at this stage, the PNP viewer's",
    "wire tap and web server (PEI-598/PEI-599). Serves the packet viewer on",
    "TCP 8081.",
    "",
    "Identity is SYSTEM, deliberately: this deviates from the atriumd rule",
    "that nothing listening on a port runs as SYSTEM. jack's explicit call",
    "(PEI-599, 2026-08-31) for the PNP development phase — the daemon needs",
    "raw packet capture anyway and predates any user; revisit the split",
    "(capture child vs server child) when PNP approaches shipping.",
    "",
    "Readiness 0 = notify: pnpd sends READY=1 once the tap and listener are",
    "up. RestartPolicy 2 = always."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\pnpd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/pnpd" },
        { "name": "Triggers", "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 2 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "PNP viewer" },
        { "name": "Description", "type": "sz", "data": "Network observation and the PNP viewer: wire tap and web UI on port 8081" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
